\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Staggered signs in low dimension}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{In one dimension the directional sign is #{1}. The
[staggered operator](fdip-014Q) is the centered difference
on the internal field. In two dimensions the first sign is
#{1}, while the second is #{(-1)^{x_1}}. It alternates along
the first coordinate when its period is even.}

\p{If the first period is odd, the same formula on the chosen
representatives still assigns a sign to each site. Both
#{x_1=N_1-1} and #{x_1=0} then have sign #{+1}. The signs
fail to alternate on the closing edge. On the covering lattice
the values at #{x_1} and #{x_1+N_1} are opposite, so the
alternating sign there does not descend to that torus.}
